nano-blk (0.1.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Build on kernels older than 6.9 (Ubuntu 24.04's GA kernel is 6.8):
    blk_mq_alloc_disk() took no queue_limits argument there, so the DKMS
    build failed and the postinst error left nano-blk-dkms unconfigured.
    Add nano_blk_compat.h, which applies the limits with blk_queue_*().

